  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 325 AM CDT Fri Aug 14 2026\n\nThe active pattern looks to continue as we head into Sunday and \nearly next week, within strong and persistent west-northwest flow \naloft. Guidance suggests more than a few shortwaves will progress \nthrough the mean flow aloft, with a near daily threat for showers \nand thunderstorms across the area. That said, the transition from \nsouthwesterly to west-northwest flow aloft, the area loses it \nmonsoonal moisture tap. This leads to PWATs falling below the highly \nanomalous levels seen much of the past few days. Still, with strong \nflow aloft and adequate instability, some threat for strong to \nsevere storms will likely continue into early next week as well.\n\nTemperatures look to remain near to below average each day for \nSunday and into next week, with daily highs in the upper 70s to \nlower 80s. The exception to this looks to be Tuesday at this time, \nwith strong warm advection ahead of an approaching frontal boundary \nboosts highs into the upper 80s to near 90 degrees. Regardless, the \nupcoming week looks to continue to be a reprieve from the hot \nconditions we saw earlier this week.",
